        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Friedrich Ratzel\n- Organizations: Nazi Party\n- Concepts: Blood and soil\n- Events: World War II\n\nFacts:\n- Friedrich Ratzel was a German geographer and ethnographer.\n- Friedrich Ratzel became notable for first using the term \"Blood and soil.\"\n- \"Blood and soil\" was a slogan that emerged from this idea.\n- The Nazi Party supported the most extreme form of the \"Blood and soil\" concept until the end of World War II.",
